# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo reads it
# when archiving a release. Two rules keep it honest, both tested in
# tests/test_citation.py:
#
#   - `version` must equal visbench.__version__, so a release cannot ship a
#     citation for the version before it.
#   - the `doi` below is the CONCEPT DOI — the one that always resolves to the
#     newest release, and which therefore never changes here. A version DOI
#     belongs in a paper reporting numbers from one specific version, not in
#     this file, which is read by someone citing "VisBench" rather than one
#     archive. Zenodo mints both per release; do not swap this for the latter.
#
# The prior work whose protocols VisBench reuses is credited in NOTICE and at
# the point of use in the code; it is deliberately not duplicated here, where a
# stale author list would be worse than a pointer.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use VisBench in your research, please cite it as below.
title: "VisBench: probing vision backbones across high-, mid- and low-level tasks"
abstract: >-
  VisBench is a unified library for probing vision backbones — DINOv2, CLIP,
  timm CNNs and ViTs, or a custom nn.Module — across high-level, mid-level and
  low-level computer vision tasks through one get_backbone() / get_probe() API.
  Fifteen probes span object and scene classification, retrieval, semantic and
  generic segmentation, detection, depth, surface normals, geometric
  correspondence, mid-level similarity, texture and occlusion edges, 2D
  keypoints, corners, and gradient orientation. Every run writes a
  structured record under an additive-only schema, and explicit comparability
  rules decide which records may be ranked together, so a number always travels
  with the conditions that produced it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Turhan Can
    family-names: Kargın
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6751-4773"
repository-code: "https://github.com/turhancan97/VisBench"
url: "https://turhancan97.github.io/VisBench/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21822684"
license: MIT
version: 0.16.0
date-released: '2026-09-05'
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - representation learning
  - probing
  - benchmark
  - foundation models
  - self-supervised learning
  - vision transformers
